 "query": "Prepare a one-page briefing for a meeting with Stripe on 17 November 2026. Cover what changed in the last 30 days (news, launches, hires, deals), cite a source URL for every fact, and end with three open questions to ask.",
 "briefing": "# Stripe Briefing: 16 October to 15 November 2026\n\n## Summary\n\nNo verified information about Stripe was retrieved for the 30-day window in any of the four categories: news, product launches, hires, or deals. Every search returned \"No valid search results found,\" and no primary page could be read directly. The absence of results therefore reflects a retrieval failure, not confirmed inactivity at Stripe. This briefing contains no facts about Stripe's activity in the window. Before the 17 November meeting, the four categories below should be checked directly against the primary sources listed in the Sources section.\n\n## News\n\nNo news items about Stripe dated 16 October to 15 November 2026 were retrieved. Searches covering company news, financial results, valuation or tender offers, regulatory actions, lawsuits, licensing, outages, security incidents, geographic expansion, and statements by Patrick Collison or John Collison all returned no results.\n\nStripe's official newsroom and press pages were not successfully read, so they remain the first place to verify. See [1] and [4] in the Sources section.\n\n## Product Launches\n\nNo product launches, feature releases, or product announcements were retrieved for the window. This includes payments, Billing, Invoicing, Connect, Treasury, Issuing, Radar, Tax, and Terminal. Searches for stablecoin and crypto infrastructure, agentic commerce and AI tools, API version releases, breaking changes, and pricing or availability changes also returned no results.\n\nThe API changelog and the Stripe blog were not successfully read. These are the most likely sources for any dated product or API changes and should be checked before the meeting. See [2] and [3] in the Sources section.\n\n## Hires and Leadership\n\nNo executive hires, notable hires, board appointments, departures, or C-suite changes at Stripe were identified for the window. Searches covering chief officer appointments, departures, board changes, leadership announcements, and former-executive hires all returned no results. No names, titles, or dates are included because none were verified.\n\nStripe's newsroom and LinkedIn company page would be the primary places to confirm any leadership change. See [1] in the Sources section.\n\n## Deals\n\nNo acquisitions, acqui-hires, investments, funding rounds, tender offers, secondary sales, strategic partnerships, customer wins, or regulatory approvals tied to deals were retrieved for the window. Searches covering Stripe acquisitions, partnerships with banks or stablecoin firms, funding and valuation, and companies acquired by or investing in Stripe all returned no results.\n\nSEC EDGAR was not searched successfully. Form D filings and other regulatory records would be the most reliable check for funding or secondary transactions. Stripe is privately held, so it does not file the periodic reports public companies file, which limits what EDGAR is likely to show.\n\n## Open Questions for the Meeting\n\n1. Which API, product, or pricing changes shipped between 16 October and 15 November 2026 that our integration team should plan around, and where are they documented?\n2. Has Stripe made any leadership changes, acquisitions, or partnership commitments in this period that have not yet been announced publicly, and how might they affect our relationship or roadmap?\n3. Which stablecoin and agentic commerce initiatives are in production today, and which remain in testing or planning?\n\n## Verification Steps Before 17 November\n\n- Check the Stripe newsroom and blog for posts dated 16 October to 15 November 2026.\n- Review the API changelog for dated entries in the window.\n- Search LinkedIn and Stripe's official social accounts for leadership announcements.\n- Search Reuters, Bloomberg, the Financial Times, The Information, and TechCrunch for Stripe coverage in the window.\n- Check SEC EDGAR for any Stripe-related filings, such as Form D.\n\nEach of these checks should be recorded with a dated URL before any item is presented as fact.\n\n### Sources\n\n[1] Stripe Newsroom (not successfully retrieved; verification source): https://stripe.com/newsroom\n[2] Stripe Blog (not successfully retrieved; verification source): https://stripe.com/blog\n[3] Stripe API Changelog (not successfully retrieved; verification source): https://docs.stripe.com/changelog\n[4] Stripe Press (not successfully retrieved; verification source): https://stripe.com/press",
